# Spec 012 T7.4, automatic (spec 013): level 1 (made in Tiled) scrolling, the bonus level (built in code), the flip
# test, then the replay, which must play exactly as on the PC and at 60 Hz.
# PC:      nnh run platformer --pc --script examples/platformer/tests/level.nnhs
# Console: nnh run platformer --script examples/platformer/tests/level.nnhs   (Homebrew Launcher open, press Y)
# Screenshots are taken outside the replay (a screenshot frame is slow on the console). About 40 seconds.
#
# The replay's checksum lines below are the PC's (pc-debug). They change whenever the level, the bonus level, the
# player's physics or the replay's script change: run `PLATFORMER_DEMO=replay NNH_EXIT_AFTER_FRAMES=920
# build/pc-debug/examples/platformer/platformer.exe` and copy its `replay: ... sum` lines here (the last one up
# to its colon). The ctest
# platformer_replay_matches_script fails until they match. Last regenerated by spec 022 T6.3: each turret has a barrel
# child entity aimed in the 8 directions; bullets leave from its muzzle point; the turret state hashes the barrels'
# world transforms; every sum changed, the x, y and coins columns did not. (Before: spec 020 T8.2: a taken coin bursts
# into four sparkle entities (spawned, faded by a tween, destroyed from the tween's callback), and each sample's
# checksum gained the level world's live entity count and a hash of the live entities' slots (not their generations:
# those carry the play before the replay, which a restart doesn't reset), so every sum changed (the bonus level's
# too): the console must reproduce every spawn and destroy. The x, y and coins columns did not change: sparkles have
# no body. (Before: spec 019 T8.2, the turrets; spec 020's stage 6 moved coins,
# turrets and bullets into a world and a pool with these lines unchanged.))
fail-on "] E "
fail-on "replay: stopped"
fail-on "replay: 60 Hz FAIL"

# Level 1: the start (camera at the left edge), then the run of the replay with the buttons: the camera follows,
# the hills and clouds scroll slower than the ground (parallax), coins are taken.
wait 30
screenshot level1-start
press RIGHT
wait 40
tap A            # up onto the first plank
wait 88
tap A            # over the first pit
wait 148
tap A            # over the second pit
wait 50
screenshot level1-parallax
wait 57
tap A            # onto the bridge
wait 40
screenshot level1-bridge
release RIGHT

# The bonus level (SELECT), built in code.
tap SELECT
wait 30
press RIGHT
wait 60
screenshot bonus
release RIGHT

# The flip test (SELECT twice: bonus -> benchmark -> flips), then back to level 1 (SELECT).
tap SELECT
wait 10
tap SELECT
wait 30
screenshot flips
tap SELECT
wait 30

# The replay (X): level 1 for 600 frames, then the bonus level for 300, no buttons. Each checksum line must be
# the PC's; the game judges 60 Hz itself (a frame over 25 ms missed) and logs PASS or FAIL on the last line.
tap X
expect "replay: started" 10
expect "replay: 60 level1 x 121 y 242 coins 1 sum 24157F9E" 120
expect "replay: 120 level1 x 226 y 210 coins 5 sum 104F45AC" 120
expect "replay: 180 level1 x 331 y 213 coins 5 sum F5960502" 120
expect "replay: 240 level1 x 436 y 226 coins 5 sum 47EEE513" 120
expect "replay: 300 level1 x 541 y 226 coins 5 sum E75B36CF" 120
expect "replay: 360 level1 x 646 y 242 coins 5 sum 4FD2991F" 120
expect "replay: 420 level1 x 751 y 202 coins 5 sum FF0D0210" 120
expect "replay: 480 level1 x 856 y 210 coins 10 sum 21A9AEE5" 120
expect "replay: 540 level1 x 891 y 242 coins 10 sum E83994ED" 120
expect "replay: 600 level1 x 950 y 210 coins 10 sum 0789E72C" 120
expect "replay: 660 bonus x 122 y 144 coins 0 sum 476B2ECD" 120
expect "replay: 720 bonus x 227 y 178 coins 0 sum 9D8D7F7D" 120
expect "replay: 780 bonus x 332 y 134 coins 0 sum 6F069DC5" 120
expect "replay: 840 bonus x 437 y 162 coins 0 sum 56B8179C" 120
expect "replay: done 900 frames sum E445E8B2: 60 Hz PASS" 120
wait 15
screenshot replay-result
end
